Subject: [PATCH] arm64: unaligned atomics: fixup for the Load128 write-back

The 128-bit load is made single-copy atomic by storing the pair straight
back with stlxp. Only the ldaxp had an exception table entry, so when the
page is mapped read-only (a copy-on-write page after fork, say) the store
faults with no fixup and the kernel oopses instead of returning the fault
to the emulation, which then kills the process. Add an entry for the
store pointing at the same exit.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/unaligned_atomic.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/unaligned_atomic.c
@@ -129,10 +129,11 @@
 
   uaccess_enable_privileged();
   asm volatile("1: ldaxp %[ResultLower], %[ResultUpper], [%[Addr]]\n"
-               "   stlxp %w[Tmp], %[ResultLower], %[ResultUpper], [%[Addr]]\n"
+               "3: stlxp %w[Tmp], %[ResultLower], %[ResultUpper], [%[Addr]]\n"
                "   cbnz %w[Tmp], 1b\n"
                "2:\n"
                _ASM_EXTABLE_UACCESS_ERR(1b, 2b, %w[ret])
+               _ASM_EXTABLE_UACCESS_ERR(3b, 2b, %w[ret])
                : [Tmp] "=&r"(Tmp), [ResultLower] "=&r"(Lower), [ResultUpper] "=&r"(Upper), [ret] "+r"(ret)
                : [Addr] "r"(Addr)
                : "memory");
